            title: '10 Card Regrets Poker',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '10 Card Regrets is a split-pot poker variant. 2-5 players. 52-card deck. Players build TWO open 5-card hands simultaneously: a Low hand and a High hand. Dealt 2 cards at a time, must assign each to Low or High (irrevocable). Cards revealed after assignment. 5 dealing rounds with betting between each. Pot split: best High hand + best Low hand.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'A split-pot poker variant in which each player builds two five-card hands (low on the left, high on the right) with irrevocable assignment. Documented as a home or informal variant for two to five players; no specific inventor or region is given in the primary source.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
